# search: tools/searchcheck.py's session (not a DOS golden: it has a test's cheat, format 6),
# recorded by the port from this script from the saved game setup/plain-debris writes (a new
# character on level 1). "Journey Onward" and the first saved game; then the test's cheat goto
# 1 27 34, a teleport within the level onto (27,34), a diagonal tile open to the north east,
# whose wall runs through the middle of the square, so the player does not fit there.
# do_teleport's find_good_x_and_y then tries the two squares the diagonal opens onto, east first:
# (28,34), open floor, where the player fits. (28,34) is in the column after the start's, whose
# bits in the visited table the original never clears; with them set the search passes it by
# and ends on (27,36); with the whole table cleared the player lands on (28,34)
3000 key enter         # Journey Onward
4500 key enter         # the first saved game
9000 cheat goto 1 27 34
